From e09e76373b6ad08a9a50c3dc87d4aedcb00fd29c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ragavan <rramasamy@maxlinear.com>
Date: Mon, 22 Jun 2026 06:20:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] WLANRTSYS-102520 Restrict prune_sta to MLO-enabled BSS and ML
 STAs only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The function mxl_clean_exiting_sta_entry_by_mac(), called from
mxl_hostapd_prune_sta(), was iterating over all BSSes and removing
any existing STA entry matching the incoming MAC address — regardless
of whether the BSS had MLO enabled or whether the STA was an ML STA.

This caused a unexpected AP_STA_DISCONNECTED event for legacy (non-MLD)
STAs when they sent an Auth Request after receiving a
BSS Transition Management Request (BTM_REQ). The prune path would
forcefully remove the legacy STA.

Fix this by adding two guards in mxl_clean_exiting_sta_entry_by_mac():
  - Skip any BSS that does not have MLO enabled.
  - Skip the STA removal if the STA is not an ML STA.

This restricts the prune logic to its intended scope — cleaning up
stale MLD STA entries across affiliated links during MLO reassociation
— and prevents it from incorrectly evicting legacy STAs that are
undergoing BSS transition steered by the AP.

Signed-off-by: ragavan <rramasamy@maxlinear.com>
---
 src/ap/mxl_utils.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ap/mxl_utils.c b/src/ap/mxl_utils.c
index 72e96fcc2..e2e7e106c 100644
--- a/src/ap/mxl_utils.c
+++ b/src/ap/mxl_utils.c
@@ -89,12 +89,15 @@ static int mxl_clean_exiting_sta_entry_by_mac(struct hostapd_iface *iface, void
 	for (j = 0; j < iface->num_bss; j++) {
 		hapd = iface->bss[j];
 
+		if (!mxl_is_mlo_enabled(hapd->conf))
+			continue;
 		sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, data->addr);
 		if (!sta)
 			sta = mxl_ap_get_sta_by_non_ap_mld_mac(hapd, data->addr);
 
 		if (sta && sta != data->new_sta_entry) {
-
+			if (!mxl_mlo_is_ml_sta(sta))
+				continue;
 			if (hapd->conf->wpa && mxl_check_sa_query(hapd, sta, 0))
 				return 1;
 
